(1172470, 145122, 8284, '<td valign="top">Wow! Placed much higher than I expected to, so I''m very happy, especially since this is only my 2nd challenge entry.<br/> <br/>First of all, the composition is exactly as found in my attic, so the background is what it is.  No names have been changed to protect the innocent (except to call it a mouse).  Surprised no one caught the text on the RAT trap, but WRD just doesn''t seem to have the same impact...  Anybody feel a little less sympathy for my "model", knowing that he''s about 14" long?<br/> <br/>Shot in near darkness.  Camera flash assisted by a weak flashlight.  Many thanks for all the positive comments, and for those who "got" the image.</td>', 'Wow! Placed much higher than I expected to, so I''m very happy, especially since this is only my 2nd challenge entry. First of all, the composition is exactly as found in my attic, so the background is what it is.  No names have been changed to protect the innocent (except to call it a mouse).  Surprised no one caught the text on the RAT trap, but WRD just doesn''t seem to have the same impact...  Anybody feel a little less sympathy for my "model", knowing that he''s about 14" long? Shot in near darkness.  Camera flash assisted by a weak flashlight.  Many thanks for all the positive comments, and for those who "got" the image.', '2005-02-16 00:30:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1172473, 145032, 17203, '<td valign="top">Congrats on yet another top 10, Brad. *yawn*<br/>Guess you had a leg up on the competition, huh? Man, I wish I could''ve found something like this. Oh wait... I did. ;-)<br/> <br/><a href="//www.dpchallenge.com/image.php?IMAGE_ID=147635" rel="nofollow" target="_blank"><img alt="'' . substr(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/17203/thumb/147635.jpg'', strrpos(''//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/17203/thumb/147635.jpg'', ''/'') + 1) . ''" border="0" src="//images.dpchallenge.com/images_portfolio/17203/thumb/147635.jpg"/></a></td>', 'Congrats on yet another top 10, Brad. *yawn*Guess you had a leg up on the competition, huh? Man, I wish I could''ve found something like this. Oh wait... I did. ;-) ', '2005-02-16 00:31:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(1172474, 145061, 31738, '<td valign="top">Good work, Congrats!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-02-21 02:21:44.</i></td>', 'Good work, Congrats!', '2005-02-16 00:31:04.000000', '2005-02-21 02:21:44.000000', 0),
(1172477, 144913, 27847, '<td valign="top">4th Challenge and a Red, now that''s something to talk about! Very powerful photo!<br/> <br/>Congrats on the ribbon.</td>', '4th Challenge and a Red, now that''s something to talk about! Very powerful photo! Congrats on the ribbon.', '2005-02-16 00:31:48.000000', NULL, 0),
(1172484, 145119, 93, '<td valign="top">Hehehe..  great comments everyone. Enjoyed every last one of them.<br/> <br/>1. Yes, we''re bad actors... but hell, I tried.<br/> <br/>2. Next time I have a good idea, I''m not going to hum and haw about it until the night of turnover, and then rush outside and snap off a quick picture. lol.  But boy, did Breeanna and I have fun doing it.<br/> <br/>3. No child was harmed in the making of this photo, but a couple of knees were. Ouch.<br/> <br/>4. 20 comments on a mid-range shot. Not too shabby.<br/> <br/>Anyway, thanks again everyone.. until next time.</td>', 'Hehehe..  great comments everyone. Enjoyed every last one of them. 1. Yes, we''re bad actors... but hell, I tried. 2. Next time I have a good idea, I''m not going to hum and haw about it until the night of turnover, and then rush outside and snap off a quick picture. lol.  But boy, did Breeanna and I have fun doing it. 3. No child was harmed in the making of this photo, but a couple of knees were. Ouch. 4. 20 comments on a mid-range shot. Not too shabby. Anyway, thanks again everyone.. until next time.', '2005-02-16 00:32:40.000000', NULL, 0),
