(1172586, 144170, 21816, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by srbrubaker:</b></div><hr/><i> I get it, It''s a blood orange!  The blood is convincing.  I know this is an almost ridiculous quibble, but it looks like a cheap knife - one that could not cut through a tomato.  And this makes me fear it ever-so-much less.  This loss of respect for the instrument causes the photo''s impact to unravel quickly.  As a rule I hate gore in photos, but the humor - intended or not- makes up for this. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Hmmm....must admit it''s a small stay sharp knife! I figured a machete may be a little large! Thanks for the tip!</td>', 'Originally posted by srbrubaker: I get it, It''s a blood orange!  The blood is convincing.  I know this is an almost ridiculous quibble, but it looks like a cheap knife - one that could not cut through a tomato.  And this makes me fear it ever-so-much less.  This loss of respect for the instrument causes the photo''s impact to unravel quickly.  As a rule I hate gore in photos, but the humor - intended or not- makes up for this.   Hmmm....must admit it''s a small stay sharp knife! I figured a machete may be a little large! Thanks for the tip!', '2005-02-16 00:49:18.000000', NULL, 0),
