(1188764, 145170, 17801, '<td valign="top">Folks, I''m the fellow who wrote the previous message with all those links.  I did note what I felt were strong similarities, but I have it on very good authority that this is truly one of those coincidences that just happens when you have some millions of digital cameras sold to millions of photographers through out the world.<br/>Just like people, it''s very rare to find what appears to be an identical twin who is not related through blood, but on occasion it just happens.<br/>I was originally shocked at the striking similarities between my own photo and this one, but on discovering this Moose was also flattened by the chilling likeness.<br/>I truly believe that he is a good person, with a good heart, and had not had prior knowledge of my image, thereby thinking and going through great lengths to turn this visualization into a truly original work of his own art.<br/>Moose, I commend you on your brilliance and creative work, and the trouble your went through to bring it all together.  A job well done, and a ribbon well deserved.<br/>Please accept my apology for posting before making the effort to speak to you first.  You have been polite and forth coming, and I feel terrible to have caused you any ageist as a result of my swiftness of text and slowness of thought.<br/>Brian D. Watters</td>', 'Folks, I''m the fellow who wrote the previous message with all those links.  I did note what I felt were strong similarities, but I have it on very good authority that this is truly one of those coincidences that just happens when you have some millions of digital cameras sold to millions of photographers through out the world.Just like people, it''s very rare to find what appears to be an identical twin who is not related through blood, but on occasion it just happens.I was originally shocked at the striking similarities between my own photo and this one, but on discovering this Moose was also flattened by the chilling likeness.I truly believe that he is a good person, with a good heart, and had not had prior knowledge of my image, thereby thinking and going through great lengths to turn this visualization into a truly original work of his own art.Moose, I commend you on your brilliance and creative work, and the trouble your went through to bring it all together.  A job well done, and a ribbon well deserved.Please accept my apology for posting before making the effort to speak to you first.  You have been polite and forth coming, and I feel terrible to have caused you any ageist as a result of my swiftness of text and slowness of thought.Brian D. Watters', '2005-02-22 16:58:18.000000', NULL, 0),
